you keep that information?

00:35:24.842 --> 00:35:26.300
This is the kind
of technology that

00:35:26.300 --> 00:35:29.420
will help your risk managers.

00:35:29.420 --> 00:35:32.150
So I do not want to leave you
without a parting thought.

00:35:35.840 --> 00:35:37.570
At the end of these
discussions, you

00:35:37.570 --> 00:35:39.784
are faced with
executives that have

00:35:39.784 --> 00:35:42.200
to decide whether they go to
the cloud or not go to cloud,

00:35:42.200 --> 00:35:45.020
a very confusing decision.

00:35:45.020 --> 00:35:48.020
And I, since a few
weeks, recommend now

00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:55.380
to divide the decision process
into four different steps.

00:35:55.380 --> 00:36:00.260
The first is to make a purely
technical risk assessment.

00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:03.230
Where is your data
going to be safer

00:36:03.230 --> 00:36:06.080
from a purely technical
point of view?

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:08.480
And I'm quite confident,
very confident actually,

00:36:08.480 --> 00:36:10.880
that this process will
lead to the direction

00:36:10.880 --> 00:36:13.070
we talked about in
the last few minutes.

00:36:13.070 --> 00:36:16.340
Then, engage into
a legal assessment.

00:36:16.340 --> 00:36:19.010
What does the law
really require?

00:36:19.010 --> 00:36:20.910
And as we've discussed
about the GDPR,

00:36:20.910 --> 00:36:23.420
it will unify the legal
landscape in Europe.

00:36:23.420 --> 00:36:25.550
It has very clear expectations.

00:36:25.550 --> 00:36:27.740
The discussions, the
legal discussions

00:36:27.740 --> 00:36:32.530
are actually getting
much easier by the month.

00:36:32.530 --> 00:36:35.920
Then, make a
political assessment.

00:36:35.920 --> 00:36:37.840
There are a number
of countries, today,

00:36:37.840 --> 00:36:41.620
that are passing laws to
keep the data in country.

00:36:41.620 --> 00:36:44.440
And you need to be sure
that your cloud provider can

00:36:44.440 --> 00:36:46.160
cope with these demands.

00:36:46.160 --> 00:36:48.820
These countries, you
know them, two years ago,

00:36:48.820 --> 00:36:53.460
Russia, six months ago, China.

00:36:53.460 --> 00:36:55.980
And our teams are paying
a lot of attention

00:36:55.980 --> 00:37:00.120
to a couple of other
countries in the central parts

00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:02.280
of the world, the Middle
East, at the moment,

00:37:02.280 --> 00:37:05.820
where these decisions
could also take place.

00:37:05.820 --> 00:37:07.120
You get the picture.

00:37:07.120 --> 00:37:09.840
Data location laws
are very rarely

00:37:09.840 --> 00:37:13.290
meant to improve the
privacy of the data.

00:37:13.290 --> 00:37:16.950
Nevertheless, you need to remain
operational in these countries.

00:37:16.950 --> 00:37:20.370
Can your cloud provider
guarantee the security

00:37:20.370 --> 00:37:22.650
of the data while,
at the same time,

00:37:22.650 --> 00:37:25.990
satisfying the expectations
of these regulators?

00:37:25.990 --> 00:37:28.120
An important assessment.

00:37:28.120 --> 00:37:31.860
Finally, the
cultural assessments,

00:37:31.860 --> 00:37:33.814
you might be faced
with reactions

00:37:33.814 --> 00:37:35.480
like I see a lot in
France, for example.

00:37:35.480 --> 00:37:36.430
I'm a French company.

00:37:36.430 --> 00:37:39.290
I want my data to
remain in France.

00:37:39.290 --> 00:37:41.967
Or you have unions that have
expectations for the data

00:37:41.967 --> 00:37:42.800
to remain in France.

00:37:42.800 --> 00:37:45.710
Or your data is deemed
national treasure.

00:37:45.710 --> 00:37:47.510
Very fine, these are
very good reasons

00:37:47.510 --> 00:37:51.680
why you might not be able
to get the data outside.

00:37:51.680 --> 00:37:54.740
But make sure that, when you go
through your decision process,

00:37:54.740 --> 00:37:57.500
you clearly make a
distinction between these four

00:37:57.500 --> 00:38:00.710
different levels and
prioritize them accordingly

00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:02.152
in your decision.

00:38:02.152 --> 00:38:04.610
This is the last thing I want
to say before introducing you

