of services that are
very, very, high level,

00:40:16.270 --> 00:40:19.090
fully managed services
that abstract away

00:40:19.090 --> 00:40:22.480
a lot of complexity of managing
your own infrastructure

00:40:22.480 --> 00:40:25.240
and your own services, a very,
very high level of abstraction,

00:40:25.240 --> 00:40:27.100
a very, very high
level of automation.

00:40:27.100 --> 00:40:28.750
That allows your
engineers to focus

00:40:28.750 --> 00:40:31.300
on what's really important
to your organization

00:40:31.300 --> 00:40:34.540
and try to provide
value, which accelerates

00:40:34.540 --> 00:40:36.980
your base of innovation,
allows you to iterate,

00:40:36.980 --> 00:40:38.950
allows you to delight
your customers,

00:40:38.950 --> 00:40:43.300
allows you to focus
on your customers.

00:40:43.300 --> 00:40:45.280
And I'm delighted to
present George, here,

00:40:45.280 --> 00:40:49.006
from Philips, who is going
to talk about how Philips has

00:40:49.006 --> 00:40:50.380
implemented Google
Cloud Platform

00:40:50.380 --> 00:40:53.530
and solved their issues when
